WEBVTT

00:04.850 --> 00:07.250
New
Mathematics 2

00:05.170 --> 00:08.640
Koishikawa-san, what's Karen Middle like?

00:08.640 --> 00:10.360
I'm not sure how to answer that.

00:10.630 --> 00:12.920
It's not much different from here.

00:12.920 --> 00:14.340
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:14.340 --> 00:17.070
A b-boyfriend? No way!

00:17.070 --> 00:19.990
What? There's no way you're not 
popular! Look how pretty you are.

00:21.330 --> 00:24.580
No way. I'm unrefined and not cute at all.

00:24.950 --> 00:28.500
Why did you transfer in at 
this time of year, anyway?

00:29.010 --> 00:33.080
Oh... Because I injured my leg.

00:33.080 --> 00:36.240
Commuting all the way to the 
next town over got too difficult,

00:36.240 --> 00:38.050
so I came here since it's closer to home.

00:38.660 --> 00:40.960
O-O-Oh, I see!

00:40.960 --> 00:45.150
S-S-Sorry, Koishikawa-san! 
She's tactless sometimes.

00:45.150 --> 00:46.770
Oh! No, it's fine!

00:47.060 --> 00:48.520
Don't even worry about it.

00:48.520 --> 00:52.040
Koishikawa-san. Sorry, but could 
you come to the faculty office?

00:52.040 --> 00:53.510
We need to go over some paperwork.

00:53.510 --> 00:54.900
Oh, sure!

00:55.410 --> 00:57.360
Sorry, I gotta go.

00:57.360 --> 00:58.820
Sure. See you later.

02:35.250 --> 02:40.800
<b><u>Episode 2</u>
With All of My Heart</b>

02:45.410 --> 02:47.620
<i>I can't seem to calm down.</i>

02:49.600 --> 02:54.500
<i>I wonder how Koishikawa-san feels about Shy.</i>

02:55.260 --> 02:57.990
Perhaps she's not even 
thinking about you.

02:58.560 --> 02:59.740
S-Shrimpy-san!

03:00.190 --> 03:04.200
Iko Koishikawa... To think 
she'd end up your classmate.

03:05.020 --> 03:07.120
Wh-What are you doing here?

03:07.120 --> 03:09.440
If anyone sees you, 
people will find out I'm Shy—

03:10.750 --> 03:13.530
You forgot your homework.

03:11.120 --> 03:16.670
Teru Momijiyama

03:14.070 --> 03:16.670
Th-Thank you.

03:19.830 --> 03:21.470
<i>I hope Shrimpy-san is right,</i>

03:22.070 --> 03:24.970
<i>and she doesn't think anything of it.</i>

03:26.250 --> 03:29.590
<i>What should I do?</i>

03:34.900 --> 03:36.530
Wh-What's wrong?!

03:36.530 --> 03:38.900
Oh... Whoops, I'm sorry.

03:38.900 --> 03:42.490
It's nothing. Don't worry, I'm fine.

03:42.490 --> 03:43.740
I just—

03:44.080 --> 03:45.950
How can you say you're fine?!

03:45.950 --> 03:48.540
I-I'll take you to the nurse's office!

03:48.540 --> 03:52.410
O-Okay... Thank you.

03:52.840 --> 03:54.540
C-Can you stand?

03:54.960 --> 03:56.370
I'm okay.

03:57.220 --> 04:00.870
Hey, you're the girl who 
sits next to me, aren't you?

04:00.870 --> 04:03.160
I-I'm Teru Momijiyama.

04:03.160 --> 04:06.110
Momijiyama-san, huh? Thank goodness.

04:06.110 --> 04:06.680
Huh?

04:06.980 --> 04:11.390
I'm glad my first friend here 
is someone as kind as you.

04:11.960 --> 04:13.080
You know?

04:14.350 --> 04:16.610
<b>Nurse's Office</b>

04:19.210 --> 04:22.850
Thank you very much. 
I'm feeling much better now.

04:22.850 --> 04:25.860
You should rest for a bit longer, though.

04:25.860 --> 04:27.920
I'll be in the faculty room.

04:27.920 --> 04:29.090
O-Okay.

04:31.500 --> 04:34.020
Sorry to put you through all that trouble.

04:34.020 --> 04:35.290
Oh, it's fine!

04:35.560 --> 04:39.290
My leg hurts every now and 
then, so I take painkillers.

04:39.290 --> 04:42.760
But I was so nervous about my first day 
at school this morning that I forgot.

04:44.050 --> 04:47.290
<i>If only I'd properly saved her 
from that accident...</i>

04:48.200 --> 04:50.660
<i>She wouldn't have to go through this.</i>

04:52.210 --> 04:53.730
Say, Momijiyama-san.

04:54.500 --> 04:58.870
You know, you sorta look like Shy, the hero.

05:00.000 --> 05:01.140
<i>Did she figure me out?!</i>

05:01.640 --> 05:05.610
When you called out to me on 
the stairs, it reminded me of her.

05:06.460 --> 05:09.280
I just keep getting saved left and right.

05:11.100 --> 05:15.410
I actually got this injury when Shy saved me.

05:16.590 --> 05:21.060
The sight of a hero when you're 
in a life-or-death situation...

05:21.780 --> 05:24.520
I'm sure it's super common,

05:24.520 --> 05:27.530
but when you're the one seeing 
it, it's really hard to forget.

05:29.870 --> 05:34.640
That's what crossed my mind, 
so you ended up looking like a hero.

05:36.520 --> 05:38.500
Sorry for being so awkward.

05:41.090 --> 05:42.020
Um...

05:43.450 --> 05:47.570
Koishikawa-san, do you resent Shy?

05:49.190 --> 05:50.700
Why would you ask that?

05:52.190 --> 05:54.660
I just thought that if Shy 
had saved you properly,

05:55.120 --> 05:58.870
you might not have gotten hurt.

05:58.870 --> 06:00.050
That's what everyone sa—

06:00.050 --> 06:01.000
Nope!

06:02.100 --> 06:07.050
No one could resent someone 
who works so hard for others.

06:08.600 --> 06:11.740
She definitely saved me.

06:11.740 --> 06:14.260
Just like you did earlier.

06:14.540 --> 06:15.640
You know?

06:20.520 --> 06:22.980
What?! Why are you crying?!

06:23.360 --> 06:27.220
I'm so sorry... I just 
suddenly felt really relieved.

06:28.370 --> 06:29.910
You okay?

06:29.910 --> 06:32.730
I'm sorry! I'll go wash my face!

06:34.970 --> 06:36.290
She's a bit strange...

06:38.070 --> 06:40.790
I wonder if she felt sorry for me.

06:41.940 --> 06:43.860
Now I feel bad.

06:46.380 --> 06:47.550
I...

06:54.480 --> 06:55.900
Ow...

07:15.520 --> 07:17.020
You poor thing.

07:19.370 --> 07:20.540
Who are you?

07:21.540 --> 07:23.140
Poor thing.

07:23.870 --> 07:26.460
Your heart's been locked up. It's crying.

07:27.340 --> 07:29.590
Whose fault is that?

07:30.360 --> 07:32.170
Why are you keeping it locked up?

07:32.730 --> 07:35.680
You're fine just the way you are.

07:47.380 --> 07:48.190
Now...

07:48.580 --> 07:52.750
Don't be shy. Open your heart.

07:57.660 --> 07:58.710
<i>That's right.</i>

07:58.710 --> 08:03.290
<i>To ensure that nice people like 
Koishikawa-san get to be happy,</i>

08:03.290 --> 08:07.880
<i>it's a hero's duty to be their beacon of hope.</i>

08:07.880 --> 08:09.630
<i>I think I understand that 
a little better now.</i>

08:11.390 --> 08:13.340
Sorry about that, Koishikawa-san!

08:13.340 --> 08:15.030
I didn't mean to just start crying.

08:17.120 --> 08:18.680
Koishikawa-san?

08:29.040 --> 08:32.270
This world is full of countless hearts,

08:32.800 --> 08:37.550
but so many of them are 
stuffed into tiny cages.

08:38.900 --> 08:44.080
Everyone thinks that they 
can't show their true heart.

08:45.040 --> 08:47.120
I'll destroy them all...

08:47.600 --> 08:50.500
All of the cages that keep you hidden.

08:51.210 --> 08:52.940
I mean, just look.

08:57.640 --> 09:00.740
True hearts are just so...

09:02.150 --> 09:03.730
Koishikawa-san?

09:08.760 --> 09:11.230
...beautiful just as they are.

09:14.700 --> 09:15.700
Shy.

09:17.550 --> 09:21.030
<u>Iko Koishikawa
</u>Nationality: Japanese
Likes: Heroes, kinako mochi
The girl Shy failed to save

09:21.320 --> 09:23.490
Momijiyama-san...

09:25.700 --> 09:28.960
What's happening... to me?

09:29.710 --> 09:31.250
S-Stay calm.

09:31.780 --> 09:33.260
What happened?

09:33.260 --> 09:35.050
I... I don't know.

09:35.650 --> 09:39.340
This strange boy appeared and... he...

09:39.340 --> 09:40.510
A boy?

09:42.220 --> 09:43.460
It hurts!

09:44.010 --> 09:45.650
It hurts! It hurts!

09:45.650 --> 09:47.440
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

09:47.810 --> 09:48.880
Are you okay?!

09:54.460 --> 09:57.360
<i>Teru, I've detected an 
abnormal energy signature.</i>

09:57.360 --> 09:58.330
<i>Analyzing now.</i>

09:57.360 --> 10:00.630
It hurts... It hurts... It hurts...

10:00.630 --> 10:03.250
What... is this?

10:03.250 --> 10:04.590
It's her heart.

10:06.010 --> 10:07.980
This is her heart.

10:08.470 --> 10:12.280
Filled with feelings of rage and hatred.

10:13.370 --> 10:14.340
Well?

10:14.930 --> 10:16.160
Isn't it beautiful?

10:17.070 --> 10:19.850
<i>A boy?! Where did he come from?</i>

10:19.850 --> 10:22.600
A-Are you the one who did 
something to Koishikawa-san?

10:23.080 --> 10:23.820
Yup.

10:24.360 --> 10:28.360
Her heart seemed like it 
was suffocating and in pain,

10:28.360 --> 10:30.600
so I opened it up for her.

10:31.050 --> 10:34.480
What... in the world... are you saying?

10:36.610 --> 10:37.650
<i>Teru, be careful.</i>

10:38.310 --> 10:41.040
<i>I've confirmed a psychic energy leak.</i>

10:41.040 --> 10:43.370
<i>Her heart is about to lose control.</i>

10:43.730 --> 10:45.840
Lose control?

10:45.840 --> 10:48.040
I have no idea what you're saying!

10:48.040 --> 10:51.630
<i>Remember, Teru. Remember 
what Unilord told you.</i>

10:52.050 --> 10:54.600
<i>The one in front of you 
right now is the one</i>

10:54.600 --> 10:57.260
<i>who brings forth darkness 
in people's hearts.</i>

10:57.750 --> 10:59.970
<i>He's someone we need to fight.</i>

11:01.360 --> 11:03.740
Are you and your friend sharing secrets?

11:03.740 --> 11:05.760
You sound so naughty, whispering like that...

11:05.760 --> 11:06.900
Shy.

11:06.900 --> 11:08.980
<i>He knows who I am?</i>

11:08.980 --> 11:11.580
Wh-Who are you?

11:11.580 --> 11:12.900
What are you after?

11:16.410 --> 11:17.570
I want...

11:18.220 --> 11:20.090
hearts to be freer.

11:23.950 --> 11:25.060
Koishikawa-san!

11:26.640 --> 11:29.960
I'm going to free them from 
their tiny little cages.

11:30.200 --> 11:32.420
Koishikawa-san! Hang in there!

11:34.240 --> 11:36.460
M-Momijiyama-san...

11:37.380 --> 11:38.340
No...

11:38.800 --> 11:40.550
You need to stay away...

11:47.220 --> 11:51.980
<i>Teru, that black crystal 
is her heart materialized.</i>

11:52.480 --> 11:55.040
H-Her heart materialized?!

11:55.040 --> 11:57.150
B-But how...

11:57.610 --> 12:01.070
<i>Currently, she's unable to control 
the emotion that is exposed.</i>

12:01.740 --> 12:03.450
<i>It's very likely that this emotion is...</i>

12:04.020 --> 12:06.200
<i>her hatred toward someone.</i>

12:07.030 --> 12:07.830
Right...

12:09.380 --> 12:10.360
<i>It's probably...</i>

12:10.870 --> 12:12.050
<i>me.</i>

12:12.960 --> 12:14.000
Momijiyama-san...

12:15.590 --> 12:17.590
I'm... sorry.

12:17.590 --> 12:21.880
It's all my fault... that you're 
experiencing something so scary.

12:22.140 --> 12:25.260
N-No! This isn't your fault, Koishikawa-san!

12:25.890 --> 12:27.760
This always happens...

12:27.760 --> 12:31.600
Everyone around me ends up hurt...

12:35.340 --> 12:37.870
My parents died...

12:37.870 --> 12:39.690
because they saved me.

12:42.010 --> 12:44.720
The house we lived in caught fire.

12:45.360 --> 12:50.860
My parents... got my little brother and 
me to safety first and stayed behind.

12:52.520 --> 12:54.530
Yeah, that's right...

12:55.330 --> 12:59.700
If they hadn't saved me, my father 
and mother wouldn't have died.

12:59.700 --> 13:03.720
And then... no one would've said 
bad things about Shy, either.

13:04.280 --> 13:06.050
No one would've gotten hurt.

13:06.680 --> 13:09.140
I should've been the one who died!

13:09.400 --> 13:10.210
Koishikawa-san!

13:10.210 --> 13:11.010
Stay back!

13:11.920 --> 13:14.660
My body's not listening to me anymore.

13:15.460 --> 13:16.570
At this rate...

13:17.400 --> 13:19.020
y-you'll also...

13:20.600 --> 13:23.530
When you called out to me in the hallway...

13:23.930 --> 13:26.780
It really made me happy.

13:27.260 --> 13:28.410
Truly.

13:29.460 --> 13:34.160
Don't get hurt like Shy did... 
all because of someone like me.

13:34.550 --> 13:35.730
Goodbye.

13:37.360 --> 13:39.500
<i>...her hatred toward someone.</i>

13:39.920 --> 13:42.670
<i>The one you hate is yourself?!</i>

13:45.730 --> 13:46.870
<i>Why?</i>

13:48.470 --> 13:49.510
<i>Why?</i>

13:50.350 --> 13:51.540
<i>Why?!</i>

14:01.910 --> 14:03.110
Why?

14:03.450 --> 14:06.110
Why won't you say, "Help me"?

14:06.940 --> 14:11.580
Why do you think you need to hold 
everything inside and suffer alone?

14:12.140 --> 14:13.240
Shy?

14:13.240 --> 14:18.310
Don't say you should die when people 
risked their lives to save you.

14:18.790 --> 14:20.750
If nothing else...

14:20.750 --> 14:22.770
If I'm able to save you,

14:22.770 --> 14:25.730
no wound could hurt me.

14:31.290 --> 14:32.390
Koishikawa-san!

14:34.000 --> 14:34.940
<i>No...</i>

14:36.200 --> 14:38.630
<i>Someone's going to get hurt again.</i>

14:38.630 --> 14:40.730
<i>You're going to lose someone dear to you.</i>

14:42.240 --> 14:44.640
<i>Those words are a curse.</i>

14:44.640 --> 14:46.510
<i>A curse that kills people.</i>

14:47.990 --> 14:48.950
<i>Don't say them...</i>

14:50.630 --> 14:54.580
<i>You can't say them! You can't!</i>

14:55.950 --> 14:57.040
Momijiyama-san...

15:02.190 --> 15:03.910
Help... me...

15:06.300 --> 15:07.520
Of course!

15:12.360 --> 15:13.970
Shrimpy-san! Open a gate!

15:13.970 --> 15:14.600
Roger.

15:26.830 --> 15:28.760
S-Sorry about that, Koishikawa-san!

15:28.760 --> 15:31.150
If we stayed there, the nurse's 
office would be in danger.

15:36.660 --> 15:40.170
Shrimpy-san! I... don't know what to do!

15:40.170 --> 15:42.180
<i>And you sounded so confident, too.</i>

15:42.180 --> 15:44.620
<i>Anyway, the analysis is complete.</i>

15:44.620 --> 15:46.290
<i>I know what's causing the leak.</i>

15:47.230 --> 15:48.500
<i>It's that ring.</i>

15:48.500 --> 15:51.010
<i>You need to separate her from that ring.</i>

15:51.010 --> 15:51.800
Ring?

15:52.220 --> 15:53.300
There it is!

15:53.670 --> 15:54.640
Here I go!

15:55.660 --> 15:56.640
Koishikawa-san!

15:56.970 --> 15:58.640
I'm going to save you now!

16:02.810 --> 16:03.600
Huh?

16:07.730 --> 16:09.730
<i>No way. The ring...</i>

16:10.190 --> 16:13.510
<i>I'll never be able to get the ring off now.</i>

16:14.580 --> 16:15.790
Hey, Shy.

16:16.560 --> 16:19.510
When my home was engulfed in flames...

16:19.960 --> 16:22.590
If you had been there for me then...

16:23.040 --> 16:26.130
If there had been a hero there for me...

16:27.440 --> 16:30.090
Maybe no one would've died...

16:31.520 --> 16:34.300
Shy, why weren't you there?

16:34.680 --> 16:36.930
Why didn't you come save me?

16:36.930 --> 16:38.430
<i>Teru, don't listen to her!</i>

16:38.800 --> 16:41.430
Heroes aren't fair...

16:41.680 --> 16:44.770
They won't save someone like me!

16:44.770 --> 16:48.240
<i>She's confused by all the hatred 
that ring is drawing out of her!</i>

16:48.240 --> 16:49.270
<i>If you listen to her—</i>

16:49.270 --> 16:50.030
No!

16:51.410 --> 16:53.570
I have to listen to her.

16:54.080 --> 16:57.220
If your current state is a reflection 
of what's deep within your heart,

16:57.220 --> 16:59.580
then you've been holding 
it in this whole time.

17:00.220 --> 17:02.820
You couldn't ask for help 
even if you wanted to,

17:02.820 --> 17:05.110
and you hated yourself for wanting help.

17:05.780 --> 17:09.090
I'm sure I heard it. 
I heard you ask for help.

17:09.860 --> 17:12.590
And I promised that I would save you!

17:12.590 --> 17:14.230
Koishikawa-san!

17:14.230 --> 17:18.700
You can throw all of the 
hatred within you at me!

17:19.660 --> 17:23.100
And I'll... answer you with my heart!

17:23.490 --> 17:25.230
<i>Teru?! What are you doing?!</i>

17:25.530 --> 17:29.360
It's all... It's all... the heroes'...

17:29.610 --> 17:30.730
Don't say...

17:31.980 --> 17:35.740
that you're going to save me... so lightly!

17:36.000 --> 17:38.030
You don't know anything!

17:38.070 --> 17:40.530
You have no idea how people 
who ask for help feel!

17:41.280 --> 17:43.790
"Why does everyone try to help others?"

17:43.830 --> 17:46.080
I don't need anyone to save me...

17:46.080 --> 17:47.790
I can't rely on anyone!

17:47.830 --> 17:49.250
<i>Teru! What's happening?!</i>

17:49.290 --> 17:50.960
I can't protect those important to me!

17:50.960 --> 17:52.960
"Nothing good ever comes of it."

17:53.480 --> 17:55.920
I... don't need anyone to save me!

17:54.530 --> 17:55.400
<i>Teru!</i>

18:00.000 --> 18:01.600
Hey, Grandpa.

18:03.280 --> 18:05.840
Why does everyone try to help others?

18:10.480 --> 18:15.110
Even if you help others, 
nothing good ever comes of it.

18:16.080 --> 18:20.990
Teru, you see... people can't live alone.

18:21.320 --> 18:23.980
Not even a single day. 
No matter who they are.

18:25.020 --> 18:27.750
When people live for others,

18:27.750 --> 18:30.550
that's when they feel the happiest.

18:30.550 --> 18:33.250
Because that's how God made us.

18:33.620 --> 18:35.110
Even if they die?

18:37.590 --> 18:41.180
Even if they died for someone 
else, are they happy?

18:42.160 --> 18:44.390
When someone dies, Teru,

18:44.390 --> 18:47.210
do you think there's no more 
happiness or anything else?

18:48.960 --> 18:49.890
I mean...

18:51.770 --> 18:53.020
There's nothing.

18:57.390 --> 18:59.130
They're nowhere...

19:02.880 --> 19:04.790
You're wrong about that.

19:07.440 --> 19:09.770
When someone lives for someone else's sake,

19:09.770 --> 19:12.330
they continue to live on 
in that person's heart.

19:12.860 --> 19:18.740
And then that person continues living for 
another, forging a connection of kindness.

19:18.740 --> 19:22.080
They risk their lives for that connection.

19:22.080 --> 19:24.350
At least, that's what your grandpa thinks.

19:25.200 --> 19:29.000
Teru, kindness is connected to you, too.

19:30.060 --> 19:32.410
Once you realize that,

19:33.020 --> 19:35.500
and when you connect with someone...

19:35.500 --> 19:38.570
I'm sure you'll understand what I mean.

19:45.010 --> 19:46.220
Help... me...

19:47.080 --> 19:49.590
Help me... someone...

19:50.470 --> 19:51.750
Help me...

19:52.640 --> 19:53.690
Iko...

19:53.690 --> 19:56.730
Iko! Look! Help is here!

19:58.560 --> 20:01.130
Dad! Mom!

20:01.550 --> 20:04.220
Your father and I will be all right.

20:04.220 --> 20:05.890
We'll see you soon.

20:06.490 --> 20:09.220
Until then, stay by your brother's side.

20:09.220 --> 20:12.380
No, wait... No... Wait!

20:12.380 --> 20:14.600
He'll be fine with his 
big sister by his side!

20:14.600 --> 20:16.940
No! Don't stay there!

20:17.650 --> 20:19.240
Don't leave me behind!

20:19.700 --> 20:21.900
I want to stay with you!

20:27.250 --> 20:29.540
What should I have done?

20:29.890 --> 20:33.040
Should I have never been born?

20:33.040 --> 20:35.880
If only I hadn't wished for 
someone to save me...

20:38.510 --> 20:39.550
Iko.

20:44.450 --> 20:48.300
You can't let yourself be 
tied down here anymore.

20:49.790 --> 20:54.020
Stop blaming yourself by thinking 
someone saving you is a sin you committed.

20:54.760 --> 20:59.350
Show someone your kindness.

21:00.590 --> 21:01.730
It's okay.

21:03.390 --> 21:04.450
It's okay.

21:12.220 --> 21:14.410
I've come to help you.

21:14.740 --> 21:17.750
Momijiyama-san...

21:19.600 --> 21:21.420
It's okay now.

21:22.090 --> 21:23.660
You're all right now.

21:26.490 --> 21:29.530
So stop hurting yourself so much.

21:30.650 --> 21:32.310
M-Momijiyama-san!

21:33.360 --> 21:36.850
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry! It's all my fault...

21:37.870 --> 21:41.010
I-It's okay. I'm fine.

21:44.800 --> 21:48.820
<i>Teru, did you know that 
the crystal would shatter?</i>

21:48.820 --> 21:51.200
I didn't... at all.

21:52.140 --> 21:55.470
I just had a feeling that if 
I put it close to my heart...

21:56.180 --> 21:58.290
Though it was just a hunch...

22:02.080 --> 22:03.760
Huh...

22:05.820 --> 22:07.590
Shy, eh?

22:17.320 --> 22:21.700
Um... I did something really awful to you.

22:22.440 --> 22:24.110
All this trouble because of me...

22:24.110 --> 22:25.430
I'm so sorry.

22:29.200 --> 22:32.360
My grandpa once told me,

22:32.360 --> 22:36.540
"When people live for others, 
that's when they feel the happiest."

22:37.040 --> 22:37.910
But...

22:38.280 --> 22:42.950
And when you connect through kindness, 
it'll pass on to someone else.

22:43.630 --> 22:46.430
And that's worth risking your life for.

22:47.470 --> 22:50.190
If you feel guilty, Koishikawa-san,

22:50.700 --> 22:53.180
then please pass on some 
kindness to someone else.

22:55.600 --> 23:00.440
If everyone is able to smile because of 
that, nothing could make me happier.

23:03.780 --> 23:04.680
Yeah...

23:05.780 --> 23:06.640
Okay.

23:08.200 --> 23:09.130
<i>Reporting.</i>

23:09.600 --> 23:12.050
<i>An emergency has occurred in Japan.</i>

23:12.050 --> 23:14.020
<i>Confirmed sighting of the boy in question.</i>

23:14.020 --> 23:15.280
<i>Shy took care of the matter.</i>

23:15.280 --> 23:17.430
<i>She fought with a crystallized civilian...</i>

23:19.520 --> 23:22.800
Momijiyama-san, I haven't said this to you yet...

23:22.800 --> 23:24.860
Huh? S-Said what?

23:26.750 --> 23:28.150
Thank you so much...

23:30.050 --> 23:31.330
for saving me!

23:33.000 --> 23:35.470
<i>No injuries or deaths.</i>
